Lecturer: Last week you wrote a main flow as numbered steps. A sequence diagram draws the same steps as messages.

6
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:47.000
Lecturer: Each participant gets a lifeline, a dashed line going down the page. Time runs downwards.

7
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Lecturer: An arrow from one lifeline to another is a message. Label it with what is being asked, like borrowBook.

8
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Lecturer: A solid arrow head is a synchronous call: the sender waits for the answer.

9
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:11.000
Lecturer: The dashed arrow back is the reply. You don't have to draw every reply, only the ones that matter.

